\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Sinners, turn; why will ye die?
\par God, your Maker, asks you why:
\par God, who did your being give,
\par Made you with Himself to live;
\par He the fatal cause demands,
\par Asks the work of His own hands:
\par Why, ye thankless creatures, why?
\par Will you cross His love, and die?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Sinners, turn; why will ye die?
\par God, your Saviour, asks you why:
\par God, who did your souls retrieve,
\par Died Himself, that you might live;
\par Will you let Him die in vain?
\par Crucify your Lord again?
\par Why, ye ransomed sinners, why
\par Will you slight His grace, and die?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Sinners, turn; why will ye die?
\par God, the Spirit, asks you why:
\par He who all your lives hath strove,
\par Wooed you to embrace His love;
\par Will you not His grace receive?
\par Will you still refuse to live?
\par Why, ye long-sought sinners, why
\par Will you grieve your God, and die?\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

